@startuml
!theme plain
title TASK-260715-1q4qhw — manager, start, message, stop sequence

actor User
participant "Containing app" as App
participant "Owned manager repository" as Repo
participant "NetworkExtension preferences" as Prefs
participant "NETunnelProviderSession" as Session
participant "NEPacketTunnelProvider shell" as Provider
participant "Shared adapter/coordinator" as Core

== Install/update without implicit enable ==
User -> App: install/update profile reference
App -> Repo: ensure(desiredReference)
Repo -> Prefs: loadAllFromPreferences()
Prefs --> Repo: app-scoped managers
Repo -> Repo: exact type + provider ID + owner marker predicate
alt zero owned and no lookalike
  Repo -> Prefs: save canonical disabled manager
else exactly one owned
  Repo -> Prefs: save only if canonical fields differ
else duplicate or unmarked lookalike
  Repo --> App: stable conflict; zero writes
end
Repo -> Prefs: reload all
Prefs --> Repo: fresh persisted manager
Repo --> App: validated fresh result

== Explicit enable and start ==
User -> App: enable/connect
App -> Repo: enableOwnedManager(explicitIntent)
Repo -> Prefs: fresh load, exact predicate, save enabled, reload
Prefs --> App: permission/authorization + persisted outcome
App -> Session: startTunnel(options: bounded v1 request)
Session --> App: accepted or synchronous error
Session -> Provider: startTunnel(options, completion)
Provider -> Provider: create once-only 60 s gate
Provider -> Core: start(stored reference)
Core -> Core: config -> SSH -> consumers -> settings -> reads -> usable snapshot
Core --> Provider: usable or mapped failure
Provider --> Session: completion(nil/error) exactly once
Session --> App: NEVPNStatusDidChange
App -> Session: read status (system authority)

== Read-only capability query ==
App -> Session: sendProviderMessage(v1 command)
Session -> Provider: handleAppMessage(data, responseHandler)
Provider -> Core: current generation snapshot
Core --> Provider: versioned bounded response
Provider --> App: response exactly once
App -> App: combine status + fresh provider facts

== Stop; stop during start follows the same join ==
User -> App: disconnect
App -> Session: stopTunnel()
Session -> Provider: stopTunnel(reason, completion)
Provider -> Provider: register once-only 10 s stop gate
Provider -> Core: stop(reason); reject new work
Core -> Core: cancel + reverse cleanup + clear routes
Core --> Provider: joined cleanup
Provider --> Session: stop completion exactly once
Session --> App: disconnected/invalid status

note over App,Provider
Host suspension, termination, or macOS quit removes app observers only.
It never sends stop or owns forwarding cleanup.
end note
@enduml
